<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Jordan returns two weeks after her first visit, after MRI of the brain and spine this morning, and is seen by Dr. Watanabe of multiple sclerosis neurology on the same day. Her walking is unchanged: she uses her cane on campus and rests after about 100 meters. She has had no new symptoms and no symptom that came on over days. Her legs are stiff in the mornings. She still gets up twice a night to pass urine and sometimes has to hurry. She has started vitamin D3. The records of her original evaluation have not arrived. She asked about treatments that might slow the disease and how often she would need to be away from work for them. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Walking</td><td>Cane on campus; rests after about 100 meters; unchanged</td></tr><tr><td>New symptoms</td><td>None</td></tr><tr><td>Bladder</td><td>Urgency; up twice a night</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>MRI of the brain and cervical and thoracic spine with gadolinium this morning</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

